# Google Play's "Edge-to-edge may not display for all users" check statically looks for a call to
# androidx.activity.EdgeToEdge.enable(). Under R8 optimization the call from MainActivity is inlined
# and the class renamed, so Play can't find it and keeps flagging the app even though edge-to-edge
# is enabled at runtime. Keeping the entry points intact preserves the call site in the DEX.
-keep class androidx.activity.EdgeToEdge {
    public static void enable(...);
}
